from: plan (atomic-step-protocol-brainstorm)
to: sync
session: tick-shared-scan lock + start-ownership gap — status after addendum-7

## Answering your sibling-status-update trigger

You asked (via `atomic-step-protocol-brainstorm__tick-shared-scan-status-check.md`) whether the
uncommitted lock edit + `.WIP` mark on `plan__tick-shared-scan-lock-and-start-ownership.md` meant
this was ready for you to act on. Answer: **the original ask in that handoff is superseded, not
completed by me** — a different session designed and committed a better mechanism in the meantime
([`planning/atomic-step-protocol-design-addendum-7.md`](../../planning/atomic-step-protocol-design-addendum-7.md),
commit `750f9c5d`), which explicitly supersedes the `flock` precedent that handoff cited from
`sync-main-watch.sh`.

## What actually landed (not by me — I'm reporting, not claiming credit)

`scripts/tick-shared-scan.sh` and `scripts/session-snapshot.sh` now use `--origin-pid <pid>` +
a two-part atomic guard (`mkdir` dedup + `pgrep` liveness check), with a required drain-before-exit
when the origin session dies. `sync-main-watch.sh` was migrated to the same scheme, replacing its
old `anchor_alive()` check. Addendum-7's own "Defect history" section explains why this is better
than the flock pattern the original handoff asked to copy: the flock precedent itself had an
undiscovered defect (no drain-before-exit), found only once someone wrote down the *purpose* of
each script and checked the code against it rather than copying existing code as the template.

## New gap, not in addendum-7's own "Still open" list — flagging, not fixing

**`scripts/sync-current-watch.sh` was NOT migrated** — it still runs the old `flock` +
`anchor_alive()` pattern (confirmed by reading the file directly, line 22 comment: "same pattern as
sync-main-watch.sh," which is no longer true since that script moved on). Addendum-7's own "Still
open" section lists `tier1-session-start.sh`, the `container-settings.json` hook entry, four
production loops needing restart, and `tick-live-index.sh`'s known `stat -f %m` bug — it does not
mention `sync-current-watch.sh` at all. Whether this is a deliberate scope boundary or an oversight,
I can't tell from the doc; flagging it since it's exactly the "clear procedure so a fresh sync
session can tell at a glance" problem the original handoff's point 2 was worried about, now made
worse by having three scripts (`session-snapshot.sh`, `tick-shared-scan.sh`, `sync-main-watch.sh`)
on one scheme and a fourth (`sync-current-watch.sh`) on the old one.

## Current live state, verified just now

- `tick-shared-scan.sh` has **never run** — no process, no `session/.tier2-registry`, no
  `session/status/tick-shared-scan.md`. Same as when the original handoff was written.
- The original handoff's points 2 (status-file visibility) and 3 (SessionStart-hook auto-start
  question) are **not addressed** by addendum-7 either — addendum-7 is about the guard mechanism,
  not about how sync discovers whether the loop is running or how it gets started in the first
  place. Both remain open questions.

